(Domain Adaptation x RLCT — L3 MeTTa Atoms\n\nC1 PROVEN: R_an,exp definable. Domain adaptation loss L = L_source(theta) + lambda * L_align(theta), where L_source is standard classification (analytic) and L_align is either MMD (RKHS distance, analytic with Gaussian kernel) or DANN (adversarial, piecewise-analytic via gradient reversal). Composite loss is R_an,exp definable.\n\nC2-C5 CONJECTURAL: Fiber intersection, lambda as stratum selector, U-shaped lambda*, generalization bound.\n\nMeTTa Atoms:\n\n(1) Domain adaptation is a composite loss problem:\n(|- ((--> DomainAdaptation composite-loss) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n(2) Source classification loss is R_an,exp definable:\n(|- ((--> source-loss R-an-exp-definable) (stv 1.0 0.95)))\n\n(3) MMD alignment loss is R_an,exp definable:\n(|- ((--> MMD-alignment-loss R-an-exp-definable) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n(4) DANN adversarial loss is piecewise R_an,exp definable:\n(|- ((--> DANN-loss piecewise-R-an-exp-definable) (stv 0.9 0.85)))\n\n(5) Composite loss creates intersection of source and alignment singular fibers:\n(|- ((==> (--> DomainAdaptation fiber-intersection) (stv 0.85 0.85)) ((--> composite-loss fiber-intersection) (stv 0.9 0.85)))\n\n(6) Fiber intersection increases RLCT relative to source-only:\n(|- ((==> (--> fiber-intersection rlct-increase) (stv 0.75 0.8)))\n\n(7) Alignment weight lambda acts as stratum selector:\n(|- ((==> (--> low-lambda source-dominated-stratum) (stv 0.8 0.75)))\n(|- ((==> (--> high-lambda alignment-dominated-stratum) (stv 0.8 0.75)))\n\n(8) Optimal lambda* is U-shaped = RLCT phase transition:\n(|- ((==> (--> DomainAdaptation (U-shaped (rlct lambda))) (stv 0.7 0.7)))\n\n(9) DANN gradient reversal creates minimax singular fiber:\n(|- ((==> (--> DANN minimax-singular-fiber) (stv 0.8 0.8)))\n\n(10) Generalization to target bounded by composite RLCT:\n(|- ((==> (--> low-composite-rlct good-target-generalization) (stv 0.75 0.75)))\n\n(11) Negative transfer corresponds to RLCT increase from alignment:\n(|- ((==> (--> negative-transfer rlct-increase) (stv 0.7 0.7)))\n\nCross-references: #543 (Dataset Distillation), #507 (Noisy Student), #293 (KD), #582 (Curriculum), #372 (Deep Supervision), #169 (Dropout).\n\n6 open problems: (1) Exact RLCT of MMD vs DANN, (2) Gradient reversal piecewise singularity, (3) Multi-source DA fiber product, (4) Negative transfer = RLCT increase, (5) Optimal lambda* vs domain gap, (6) Optimal transport alignment non-analytic singularities.